---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import { site } from '../content/site'
import { Image } from 'astro:assets'
---
<BaseLayout title={`${site.privacy.pageTitle} | ${site.company.name}`} description="Privacy notice draft awaiting business and provider details.">
  <header class="site-header">
    <div class="container header-inner">
      <a class="brand" href="/" aria-label={`${site.company.name} home`}>
        <Image src={site.assets.logo} alt={site.assets.logoAlt} width="280" height="140" class="brand-logo" />
      </a>
      <a class="text-link" href="/">Back to home <span aria-hidden="true">←</span></a>
    </div>
  </header>
  <main id="main" class="privacy-page">
    <nav class="contents" aria-label="Contents">
      <strong>Contents</strong>
      <ol>
        <li><a href="#controller">Who is responsible for your information?</a></li>
        <li><a href="#information">Information we collect</a></li>
        <li><a href="#purposes">How and why we use information</a></li>
        <li><a href="#lawful-bases">Our lawful bases</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sharing">Who we share information with</a></li>
        <li><a href="#transfers">International transfers</a></li>
        <li><a href="#retention">How long we keep information</a></li>
        <li><a href="#security">How we protect information</a></li>
        <li><a href="#cookies">Cookies and website analytics</a></li>
        <li><a href="#rights">Your data protection rights</a></li>
        <li><a href="#children">Children's information</a></li>
        <li><a href="#changes">Changes to this policy</a></li>
        <li><a href="#contact">Contact and complaints</a></li>
      </ol>
    </nav>
    <div class="container privacy-content">
      <p class="eyebrow"><span></span>Privacy</p>
      <h1>{site.privacy.pageTitle}</h1>
      <p class="privacy-intro">This Privacy Policy explains how LOLER Inspections collects and uses personal information when you visit <a href="https://www.loler-inspections.com/">www.loler-inspections.com</a>, contact the business, or use its lifting equipment inspection services.</p>
      <div class="privacy-details">
        <section id="controller">
      <h2>1. Who is responsible for your information?</h2>
      <p>LOLER Inspections is the trading name of <strong>Chris Rushworth</strong>, a sole trader. For the purposes of UK data protection law, Chris Rushworth is the data controller responsible for deciding how and why personal information is used in connection with the business.</p>
      <br/>
      <p>In this policy, “we”, “us” and “our” refer to Chris Rushworth trading as LOLER Inspections.</p>
      <br/>
      <div class="contact">
        <strong>Privacy contact</strong><br>
        Chris Rushworth trading as LOLER Inspections<br>
        Email: <a href="mailto:Loler-inspections@outlook.com">Loler-inspections@outlook.com</a>
      </div>
      <p>We do not currently have a Data Protection Officer. You can use the email address above for all privacy questions and requests.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="information">
      <h2>2. Information we collect</h2>
      <h3>Information submitted through the website</h3>
      <p>When you use the website contact form, we collect the information you choose to provide. This may include:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>your name</li>
        <li>your email address</li>
        <li>your telephone number</li>
        <li>your company or organisation name and</li>
        <li>the contents of your enquiry or message.</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>Information relating to inspection services</h3>
      <p>When we discuss, arrange or carry out inspection services, we may collect and use information needed to manage the work and produce inspection records. Depending on the service and the people involved, this may include:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>customer, client, site contact and responsible-person names and contact details</li>
        <li>business and site details, including equipment locations</li>
        <li>names, roles and signatures of inspectors or site representatives</li>
        <li>equipment identification, examination details, findings and inspection history</li>
        <li>photographs or other records created as part of an inspection, which may incidentally show identifiable people and</li>
        <li>correspondence, quotations, instructions and service records.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We only intend to collect information that is relevant to responding to an enquiry, providing our services, documenting inspection work or meeting applicable legal and regulatory requirements. Please do not include sensitive personal information in a website enquiry unless it is genuinely necessary.</p>
      <h3>Information collected when you visit the website</h3>
      <p>The website is hosted using Cloudflare Pages. Cloudflare may process technical information associated with delivering and securing the website, such as IP address, browser and device information, request details and security or diagnostic logs, in accordance with its service terms and privacy documentation.</p>
      <p>We use Cloudflare Web Analytics to understand general website usage. Cloudflare states that Web Analytics does not collect or use visitors' personal data. We do not use Google Analytics or advertising tracking pixels on the website.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="purposes">
      <h2>3. How and why we use information</h2>
      <p>We use personal information for the following purposes:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Responding to enquiries:</strong> to reply to questions, discuss requirements and provide information about our services.</li>
        <li><strong>Managing quotations:</strong> to prepare, send and follow up on quotations or other requests for services.</li>
        <li><strong>Providing inspection services:</strong> to arrange and carry out inspections, communicate with customers and relevant site contacts, and deliver inspection reports.</li>
        <li><strong>Maintaining inspection records:</strong> to document examinations, findings, equipment details and relevant communications, and to meet applicable health and safety, regulatory and legal requirements.</li>
        <li><strong>Managing the business:</strong> to maintain appropriate business records, deal with queries or disputes, protect our rights and keep our services secure.</li>
        <li><strong>Operating and securing the website:</strong> to host the website, monitor its general performance and protect it against misuse or malicious activity.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We may contact you again about an outstanding quotation or an enquiry you have made. We do not use website enquiry details to send newsletters or general promotional campaigns. If our use of information changes, we will update this policy and provide any additional information required by law before starting the new use.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="lawful-bases">
      <h2>4. Our lawful bases for using personal information</h2>
      <p>UK data protection law requires us to have a lawful basis for each purpose for which we use personal information. Depending on the circumstances, we rely on the following bases:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Taking steps at your request before entering into a contract, and performing a contract:</strong> for responding to service enquiries, preparing quotations, arranging work and providing agreed inspection services.</li>
        <li><strong>Legal obligation:</strong> where processing is necessary to comply with legal or regulatory duties, including applicable duties relating to the recording and reporting of thorough examinations and inspections.</li>
        <li><strong>Legitimate interests:</strong> for proportionate business administration, keeping appropriate records, following up on an outstanding quotation or enquiry, maintaining service history, protecting the business and securing the website. We consider the impact on individuals and their rights when relying on this basis.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Where we rely on legitimate interests, our interests include operating and administering the inspection business, responding to people who have contacted us, keeping evidence of work and communications, and protecting our systems. We do not use this basis to send general marketing campaigns.</p>
      <p>Where information is required to enter into or perform a contract, or is required by law, we will explain this when appropriate. If you do not provide information that is necessary for the requested service or a legal requirement, we may be unable to provide that service or complete the relevant work.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="sharing">
      <h2>5. Who we share information with</h2>
      <p>We do not sell personal information. We only disclose it where necessary for the purposes described in this policy, where we have a lawful basis, or where the law requires or permits us to do so.</p>
      <p>Depending on how you interact with us, information may be processed by the following service providers:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>StaticForms:</strong> our website contact form sends submissions to StaticForms through <a href="https://api.staticforms.dev/submit">api.staticforms.dev/submit</a>. StaticForms stores form submissions in its dashboard and sends submission notifications to our business email address.</li>
        <li><strong>Microsoft Outlook:</strong> contact form notifications and business correspondence are received at our Outlook email address. Microsoft processes information as part of providing its email service.</li>
        <li><strong>Cloudflare:</strong> provides website hosting and related security and analytics services.</li>
        <li><strong>Website developer:</strong> a developer engaged by the business may access the StaticForms dashboard and enquiry information when authorised by the business, for website administration, troubleshooting, exporting enquiry history or other instructed support. The developer is not the data controller and must handle information only under the business's instructions and appropriate confidentiality and data-processing arrangements.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We may also share relevant information with a customer, an authorised site contact, a relevant enforcing authority or another person where this is necessary to provide the inspection service or comply with a legal duty. For example, the law may require a report about a dangerous defect to be provided to the relevant enforcing authority.</p>
      <p>Service providers are permitted to process personal information only for the services they provide and subject to their applicable contractual and data protection obligations. We do not authorise them to use enquiry information for their own marketing.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="transfers">
      <h2>6. International transfers</h2>
      <p>Some of the service providers used to operate the website and handle enquiries may process information outside the United Kingdom. Where personal information is transferred internationally, the transfer must be covered by a lawful transfer mechanism under UK data protection law, such as UK adequacy regulations or appropriate safeguards.</p>
      <p>For StaticForms, the account is configured for EU data residency. StaticForms states that form submissions and related form data for EU-region accounts are stored in its AWS infrastructure in Frankfurt, Germany. EU data residency does not mean that every related processing activity takes place in the EU: StaticForms states that account information and operational request logs are processed or stored in the United States, and that notification emails are transmitted using AWS infrastructure in the United States, with Singapore configured as a failover region. Its published Data Processing Agreement describes the transfer safeguards it relies on, including Standard Contractual Clauses and the UK International Data Transfer Addendum where applicable.</p>
      <p>AI-assisted spam evaluation is disabled for the contact form. This statement describes the form's current configuration and should be reviewed if its settings change.</p>
      <p>Cloudflare and Microsoft may also process information in other countries as part of their services. Those providers' own contractual terms, privacy information and transfer safeguards apply to their processing. You can contact us using the details in this policy if you would like further information about relevant transfer safeguards.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="retention">
      <h2>7. How long we keep information</h2>
      <p>We keep personal information only for as long as it is reasonably necessary for the purposes for which it was collected, including to meet legal, regulatory, accounting or reporting requirements and to establish or defend legal claims. The period depends on the type of information and the circumstances.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Website enquiries and quotations:</strong> while an enquiry or quotation remains active and, after it has closed or become inactive, normally for up to 12 months. We will review records and securely delete or anonymise them sooner where they are no longer needed, unless there is a legitimate reason to retain them for longer.</li>
        <li><strong>Inspection reports and related records:</strong> for as long as necessary to meet applicable legal and regulatory requirements, provide an appropriate record of the inspection, deal with follow-up questions or disputes, and protect the legitimate interests of the business and its customers. The appropriate period may depend on the type of equipment, the inspection interval, the nature of any findings and other applicable obligations.</li>
        <li><strong>Business and financial records:</strong> for the period required by applicable tax, accounting and other legal requirements.</li>
        <li><strong>Website security and technical logs:</strong> for the period made available by the relevant service provider and needed for security, troubleshooting and service operation.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Where a record is subject to a legal hold, an ongoing dispute, an investigation or another valid reason for extended retention, we may keep it for longer. When information is no longer required, we will take reasonable steps to delete it securely or anonymise it.</p>
      <p>StaticForms may retain a copy of a contact form submission in its dashboard. Deleting an email from the Outlook inbox does not necessarily delete the corresponding StaticForms dashboard record or any separate export. Where we delete enquiry information, we will take reasonable steps to address the copies under our control, subject to provider processes, backup cycles and any lawful retention requirement.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="security">
      <h2>8. How we protect information</h2>
      <p>We take reasonable technical and organisational measures designed to protect personal information against unauthorised access, accidental loss, alteration or disclosure. These measures include using established service providers, encrypted connections where supported, access controls and limiting access to people who need information to perform authorised work.</p>
      <p>No method of transmitting or storing information is completely secure. If we become aware of a personal data breach affecting information for which we are responsible, we will assess it and take the steps required by data protection law, including notifying the Information Commissioner's Office or affected individuals where legally required.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="cookies">
      <h2>9. Cookies and website analytics</h2>
      <p>We do not currently use cookies on this website. Cloudflare Web Analytics is used to understand general website traffic and performance. Cloudflare states that its Web Analytics service does not collect or use visitors' personal data.</p>
      <p>We do not currently use Google Analytics, advertising pixels or similar advertising trackers. If we introduce cookies or other technologies that require consent, we will update this policy and provide an appropriate consent mechanism before using them.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="rights">
      <h2>10. Your data protection rights</h2>
      <p>Under UK data protection law, you may have the following rights in relation to your personal information:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Access:</strong> to request a copy of your personal information and certain details about how it is used.</li>
        <li><strong>Rectification:</strong> to ask us to correct inaccurate information or complete information that is incomplete.</li>
        <li><strong>Erasure:</strong> to ask us to delete your information in certain circumstances.</li>
        <li><strong>Restriction:</strong> to ask us to restrict how we use your information in certain circumstances.</li>
        <li><strong>Objection:</strong> to object to processing based on legitimate interests, where the law gives you that right. You have an absolute right to object to the use of your personal information for direct marketing.</li>
        <li><strong>Data portability:</strong> to request certain information in a structured, commonly used and machine-readable format, where the right applies.</li>
        <li><strong>Withdraw consent:</strong> where we rely on consent, you can withdraw it at any time. This will not affect processing carried out before consent was withdrawn.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>These rights are not absolute in every situation and may be subject to legal conditions or exemptions. We will explain if a right does not apply to a particular request.</p>
      <p>To exercise a right, email <a href="mailto:Loler-inspections@outlook.com">Loler-inspections@outlook.com</a>. Please provide enough information for us to identify you and understand your request. We may need to verify your identity before responding. We will normally respond within one month of receiving a valid request. This period may be extended by up to a further two months for complex or multiple requests, in which case we will explain the reason for the extension.</p>
      <p>There is normally no charge for making a request. We may charge a reasonable fee or refuse to act where a request is manifestly unfounded or excessive, as permitted by law.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="children">
      <h2>11. Children's information</h2>
      <p>Our services and website are intended for businesses and people acting in a professional or work-related capacity. We do not knowingly seek to collect personal information directly from children through the website.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="changes">
      <h2>12. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>We may update this Privacy Policy when our business, website, service providers or legal obligations change. The latest version will be published on this page, with the date of the most recent update shown at the top. If a change materially affects how we use information already collected, we will provide additional information where required by law.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="contact">
      <h2>13. Contact and complaints</h2>
      <p>If you have a question, concern or request about how we use your personal information, please contact:</p>
      <div class="contact">
        <strong>Chris Rushworth trading as LOLER Inspections</strong><br>
        Email: <a href="mailto:Loler-inspections@outlook.com">Loler-inspections@outlook.com</a><br>
        Website: <a href="https://www.loler-inspections.com/">www.loler-inspections.com</a>
      </div>
      <p>You also have the right to complain to the Information Commissioner's Office (ICO), the UK's independent data protection regulator. The ICO encourages people to raise concerns with the organisation first where possible, but you can contact the ICO directly.</p>
      <p>
        Information Commissioner's Office<br>
        Website: <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/">ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint</a><br>
        Telephone: 0303 123 1113
      </p>
    </section>
      </div>
      <a class="button" href="/">Return to LOLER Inspections</a>
    </div>
  </main>
  <footer class="site-footer">
    <div class="container footer-bottom">
      <span>{site.company.name}</span>
      <a href="/">Home</a>
    </div>
  </footer>
</BaseLayout>
